      "paragraphs": [
        "A little more clarity",
        "Tools your team can realistically license or use free (for example Canva-class design tools and accessible video editors), configured around what you already have. If you're on Adobe, we train on Adobe.",
        "Where they genuinely help, yes: drafting, repurposing and ideation are covered honestly, including where AI output needs human editing before it's publishable. For a deeper AI-at-work program, see the Prompt Engineering track.",
        "No; this track exists for exactly that team. Small batches run as intensive working sessions built around your actual upcoming content calendar.",
        "Yes. Social media training for employees runs well as a standalone session (planning, platform-fit content and posting workflow); many teams start there and add writing, design or video later."
      ],
