        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "Good questions."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Which design and video tools does the training use?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Tools your team can realistically license or use free (for example Canva-class design tools and accessible video editors), configured around what you already have. If you're on Adobe, we train on Adobe."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Does this cover using AI tools for content?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Where they genuinely help, yes: drafting, repurposing and ideation are covered honestly, including where AI output needs human editing before it's publishable. For a deeper AI-at-work program, see the Prompt Engineering track."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Our whole marketing team is two people. Is that too small a batch?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "No; this track exists for exactly that team. Small batches run as intensive working sessions built around your actual upcoming content calendar."
        },
        {
          "type": "summary",
          "text": "Can we book just the social media module as standalone training for employees?+"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Yes. Social media training for employees runs well as a standalone session (planning, platform-fit content and posting workflow); many teams start there and add writing, design or video later."
        }
